    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "net: stop using a socket once a wait reports an error",
    "user": {
      "login": "darosior",
      "id": 22457751,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDU3NzUx",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22457751?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/darosior",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "ConnMan and the HTTP server would still try to read (and send) when a wait reports ErrorEvent. This means they could still read even when a read was not requested.\r\n\r\nOn select() based platform (BSDs, macOS and Windows), ErrorEvent can be returned if a peer sends us urgent data (we register the exception set because of a Windows quirk). However we can't read that urgent data, and this means we could be continuously woken up.\r\n\r\nThere is a number of things we could do to improve the situation here (see discussions in #36761), but in the meantime fix this bug by simply disconnecting immediately upon error. For consistency, adopt the same behaviour across all callers.\r\n\r\nThis PR is an alternative to #36716.",
