      "body": "This prevents us from reading any more data after an ERR/HUP event, which is counter to how the typical TCP flow works. A half-close is a perfectly reasonable thing for a peer to do when they're done sending.\r\n\r\nI'm not opposed to this as it's clearly a reasonable defensive measure to take, but I'm nervous that the current p2p network relies on this behavior to some extent.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T16:26:05Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T16:26:06Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36953#discussion_r4668651817",
