      },
      "body": "I think this is incorrect. A half close sends a FIN, and poll() returns POLLIN for this. So this commit does not change behaviour in this case.\r\n\r\nHowever, a peer abruptly `close()`ing its connection right after sending us data may result in a RST, for which poll() returns ERR/HUP and for which we would now disconnect early. But that's hardly a \"perfectly reasonable thing to do\".\r\n\r\nI'm running some probes now to get an idea of how well we process messages in practice in each of these situations, before and after the PR.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T16:44:43Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T16:44:43Z",
